<%--
Rich_Text_Display - renders a Rich_Text value on a live page.

$value - a Rich_Text instance (NOT a string)

This is the PRINTER component Rich_Text declares, so it is almost never written by
hand: interpolating the value is enough, and jqhtml mounts this in place.

    <%= this.data.project.description %>

The unescaped interpolation below is the one place in the application where raw
markup enters the DOM, and it is correct HERE and nowhere else: Rich_Text filtered this
content through safe_html() at the trust boundary on write. That is the whole trade the
text-type system makes - one component owns the unescaped output for an encoding,
instead of every call site deciding for itself.

It runs through safe_html() (DOMPurify) AGAIN here, and that is belt-and-braces rather
than distrust of the store. The write filter is the authority; this line covers what
bypassed it - a row written by raw SQL or a migration, or a value an endpoint echoed
straight back without ever assigning it, which reaches this component unfiltered. It is
cheap, it is the literal injection point, and a second check at the one place it
matters costs nothing.

Usage (only when a printer needs an argument it cannot get by interpolation):
    <Rich_Text_Display $value=this.data.project.description />
--%>
<Define:Rich_Text_Display tag="div">
    <%!= safe_html(this.args.value.to_storage()) %>
</Define:Rich_Text_Display>
